  "summary": "Malicious code in bigops-status-selection (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a second-stage binary. It fingerprints the OS/architecture, then fetches a payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev at path /pkg/package (platform-specific variants /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe). If those fail it reconstructs the payload from DNS TXT records served under c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (with per-arch domains sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to a temp directory (.cache_\u003chex\u003e on Unix, dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows) and launched detached via cmd.exe start /b on Windows or /bin/sh -c '... \u0026' on Unix.",
  "affected": [
